('127.313.d.6.A',4,'A family in which grandparents, aunts, or uncles live with the parents and children is an:','["single-parent family", "blended family", "extended family", "nuclear family"]'::jsonb,2,'Extended families include other relatives.','original'),
('127.313.d.6.B',3,'A teacher can build a partnership with families by:','["limiting visits", "sharing only bad news", "avoiding contact", "inviting families to participate and share ideas"]'::jsonb,3,'Partnerships are two-way.','original'),
('127.313.d.6.B',4,'A family-teacher conference should focus on:','["the child''s progress and goals", "the teacher''s problems", "unrelated gossip", "other families'' private information"]'::jsonb,0,'Conferences center on the child.','original'),
('127.313.d.6.C',3,'Which method helps teachers reach families who speak another language?','["no communication", "Translated notes or an interpreter", "phone calls at midnight", "English-only notes"]'::jsonb,1,'Language access builds partnership.','original'),
('127.313.d.6.C',4,'Daily communication tools such as apps and newsletters help families:','["lose track of events", "skip conferences", "stay informed about classroom activities", "avoid the school"]'::jsonb,2,'Regular updates keep families connected.','original'),
('127.313.d.7.A',3,'Professionalism with coworkers includes:','["ignoring requests", "gossiping", "blaming others", "respectful communication and teamwork"]'::jsonb,3,'Professional teams cooperate.','original'),
('127.313.d.7.A',4,'A teacher who arrives on time, dresses appropriately, and keeps confidences shows:','["professionalism", "carelessness", "favoritism", "bias"]'::jsonb,0,'These habits show professional behavior.','original'),
('127.313.d.7.B',3,'To resolve a disagreement with a coworker, a teacher should:','["ignore it forever", "listen and look for a solution together", "argue in front of children", "complain to parents"]'::jsonb,1,'Problem solving is respectful.','original'),
('127.313.d.7.B',4,'Using ''I'' statements in a conflict helps because they:','["escalate anger", "avoid the issue entirely", "express feelings without blaming", "blame the other person"]'::jsonb,2,'I-statements reduce defensiveness.','original'),
