('127.313.d.7.D',3,'Advocating for early childhood education can include:','["cutting funding", "sharing research on its benefits with community leaders", "hiding data", "closing programs"]'::jsonb,1,'Advocates make the case.','original'),
('127.313.d.7.D',4,'Research shows high-quality early education can lead to:','["no effects at all", "lower graduation rates", "better outcomes in school and later life", "more school absences"]'::jsonb,2,'Early learning has lasting benefits.','original'),
('127.313.d.8.A',3,'A professional portfolio might include:','["unrelated photos", "a game score", "a grocery list", "a resume, lesson plans, and references"]'::jsonb,3,'Portfolios show qualifications.','original'),
('127.313.d.8.A',4,'A work sample in an early childhood portfolio could be:','["a lesson plan you wrote", "a receipt", "a recipe card", "a friend''s lesson plan"]'::jsonb,0,'Samples must be your own work.','original'),
('127.313.d.8.B',3,'When presenting a portfolio to a director, a student should:','["argue with questions", "explain each item and what it shows about their skills", "read silently", "skip items"]'::jsonb,1,'Explanations connect work to skills.','original'),
('127.313.d.8.B',4,'At the end of a portfolio presentation, a good next step is to:','["leave abruptly", "argue with comments", "ask for feedback and thank the reviewers", "ignore feedback"]'::jsonb,2,'Feedback supports growth.','original'),
('127.314.d.1.A',3,'A teacher''s emails to parents should be:','["emotional", "casual and full of slang", "careless", "professional, respectful, and clear"]'::jsonb,3,'Professional communication builds trust.','original'),
('127.314.d.1.A',4,'Educator codes of ethics require teachers to communicate with students:','["professionally and appropriately", "as personal friends", "only socially", "through private chats at midnight"]'::jsonb,0,'Boundaries protect students.','original'),
('127.314.d.1.B',3,'A teacher should contact parents promptly when a student has:','["a new haircut", "a serious injury or safety concern", "a lost pencil", "a favorite color"]'::jsonb,1,'Safety issues require quick contact.','original'),
('127.314.d.1.B',4,'Which situation requires a school to notify the community?','["a pencil sale", "a lost sock", "An emergency such as a lockdown or weather closure", "a new bulletin board"]'::jsonb,2,'Emergencies require timely notice.','original'),
('127.314.d.1.C',3,'An appropriate use of social media by a teacher is:','["friending students privately", "posting student grades", "venting about students", "sharing classroom learning tips on an approved school account"]'::jsonb,3,'Professional accounts serve learning.','original'),
('127.314.d.1.C',4,'A teacher posting a photo of students online should first:','["confirm that the district and parents allow it", "tag the students", "post immediately", "share personal addresses"]'::jsonb,0,'Permission is required.','original'),
('127.314.d.1.D',3,'A teacher who has an inappropriate relationship with a student can face:','["a raise", "loss of their teaching certificate and criminal charges", "a promotion", "an award"]'::jsonb,1,'Misconduct has severe consequences.','original'),
('127.314.d.1.D',4,'Educator misconduct in Texas is investigated through the:','["student council", "school cafeteria", "State Board for Educator Certification", "local newspaper"]'::jsonb,2,'SBEC oversees educator certification.','original'),
('127.314.d.2.A',3,'Effective verbal communication with parents includes:','["using jargon", "interrupting", "speaking harshly", "speaking clearly and respectfully"]'::jsonb,3,'Clear, respectful speech builds partnership.','original'),
('127.314.d.2.A',4,'When explaining test results to a parent, a teacher should avoid:','["unexplained technical jargon", "plain language", "clear examples", "a calm tone"]'::jsonb,0,'Plain language helps families understand.','original'),
('127.314.d.2.B',4,'A teacher says, ''So you are worried about the homework load, is that right?'' This is:','["giving an order", "checking understanding by paraphrasing", "ending the conversation", "changing the topic"]'::jsonb,1,'Restating confirms meaning.','original'),
('127.314.d.2.C',3,'A website where a teacher posts updates that others can comment on is a:','["podcast", "vlog", "blog", "wiki"]'::jsonb,2,'Blogs are posts with comments.','original'),
('127.314.d.2.C',4,'A recorded audio program that students can listen to online is a:','["blog", "infographic", "wiki", "podcast"]'::jsonb,3,'Podcasts are audio episodes.','original'),
('127.314.d.2.D',3,'A professional email to a parent should include:','["a clear subject line and polite greeting", "all capital letters", "emojis only", "no signature"]'::jsonb,0,'Format signals professionalism.','original'),
('127.314.d.2.D',4,'Before sending an email about a student, a teacher should:','["copy the whole class", "proofread and protect student privacy", "add personal opinions", "use slang"]'::jsonb,1,'Accuracy and privacy matter.','original'),
('127.314.d.2.E',3,'Teachers collaborate effectively by:','["working in isolation", "hiding materials", "sharing ideas and resources in team meetings", "criticizing publicly"]'::jsonb,2,'Collaboration improves teaching.','original'),
('127.314.d.2.E',4,'A professional learning community (PLC) is a group of teachers who:','["avoid sharing", "compete for awards", "meet only socially", "meet regularly to improve student learning"]'::jsonb,3,'PLCs focus on learning.','original'),
('127.314.d.2.F',3,'Clear assignment directions should include:','["what to do, how, and the due date", "a hidden deadline", "nothing in writing", "only the title"]'::jsonb,0,'Students need complete directions.','original'),
('127.314.d.2.F',4,'Giving feedback on a student''s work is most useful when it is:','["vague and late", "specific and timely", "only a grade", "negative only"]'::jsonb,1,'Specific feedback guides improvement.','original'),
('127.314.d.2.G',3,'To make group work fair, a teacher can assign:','["one worker", "the same job to all", "roles such as recorder and reporter", "no roles"]'::jsonb,2,'Roles share responsibility.','original'),
('127.314.d.2.G',4,'A strategy where students first think alone, then discuss with a partner, then share with the class is called:','["silent reading", "jigsaw review", "lecture-only", "think-pair-share"]'::jsonb,3,'Think-pair-share builds participation.','original'),
('127.314.d.2.H',3,'A teacher uses simple words and visuals for an English learner. This is:','["adapting communication to student needs", "ignoring the student", "lowering expectations", "teaching less content"]'::jsonb,0,'Supports make content accessible.','original'),
('127.314.d.2.H',4,'A student with a hearing impairment may need the teacher to:','["speed up speech", "face the student and use visual supports", "speak louder from behind", "avoid the student"]'::jsonb,1,'Visual access helps.','original'),
('127.314.d.3.A',3,'Digital literacy means being able to:','["avoid computers", "type only", "find, evaluate, and use information online", "copy others'' work"]'::jsonb,2,'Digital literacy is critical use.','original'),
('127.314.d.3.A',4,'Before sharing an article online, a digitally literate person checks:','["its ads", "its page color", "its font size", "the source''s credibility"]'::jsonb,3,'Credibility matters.','original'),
